WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.120
This potato is about to hit a grid of knives at nearly 40 miles an hour.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.980
If it jams, 88 more pile up behind it in 10 seconds,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.600
it's a hydro cutter and it's how factories turn potatoes into fries.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.450
It starts in a tank of water.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.360
Pump pushes water and potatoes into a pipe.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.880
Then the pipe narrows the water has to squeeze through so it speeds up and carries the potato with it.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.700
The narrowing also lines each potato up nose first dead center.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.950
Waiting at the end is a grid of thin steel blades. The first row slices the potato.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.680
ACssing row cuts every slice into sticks faster than you can blink the whole potato is through.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.860
Pass the knives, the pipe widens,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:46.100
everything slows down and the fries land on a shaking screen while the water runs back to the tank.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.580
Bldes never move fast enough, a potato cuts itself.
